# An allowlist: the build context holds only what the Dockerfile reads, so a file that
# lands in the repo folder (a HAR with a live Musora session, an agent's worktree, a
# local config) never reaches the image or the build cache unless it is let in here.
# The last matching line wins: `*` drops everything, the `!` lines let back in exactly
# the Dockerfile's inputs (go.mod and go.sum, `COPY . .` building ./cmd/drumdrop, which
# imports internal/ and web/, `COPY web/` for the web stage, entrypoint.sh), and the lines
# after them drop what can sit inside those folders. `**/` matches at any depth.
*
!go.mod
!go.sum
!cmd/
!internal/
!web/
!entrypoint.sh

# Installed packages and built output: each stage installs and builds its own.
**/node_modules
web/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.test
cmd/drumdrop/drumdrop
# Local state and secrets, in case DRUMDROP_CONFIG_DIR or a download points in here.
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
**/secret.key
**/credentials.enc
**/session.cookie
**/.env*
**/.secrets*
**/*.har
**/*.log
**/*.pid
**/*.sock
**/downloads
# Test reports `make coverage` writes for SonarQube.
**/coverage.out
**/go-test-report.json
web/coverage
# Local-only folders and config: Claude Code's (agent worktrees included), the
# brainstorm companion's, and the per-machine MCP server config.
**/.claude
**/.superpowers
**/.mcp.json
